    "title": "Look out for the wood stork, Florida - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Randi Atwood ,\n8 hours ago Happy Thursday, Florida!\nThe U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service is ready to take the wood stork off the Endangered Species List . So that's good news, isn't it?\nWell, some environmental groups say it's not time yet .\nThese wading birds — which once nested in huge numbers in Naples — are still struggling in Florida .\nAnd boy, those babies can make some noise .\nHere's more of what's happening around Florida: Right there : Florida is solid red these days. Right? Here's what the latest poll says about the next Senate and governor races .\nFill 'er up (and up): Florida gas prices surged for a second straight day , climbing 31 cents over the past two days.\nA little help: Not long ago, using AI to write a school paper was cheating. Now some Florida teachers are embracing artificial intelligence as a tool for learning. Here's how .\n(Got a Florida story idea? Pass it along to me at RAtwood@usatodayco.com.)\nThis article originally appeared on Tallahassee Democrat: Look out for the wood stork, Florida\n18",
